      "sample_index": 1,
      "text": "To find out which month the 25th battery replacement will occur, we need to calculate the day it falls on and determine the month. Consider that the first replacement is in May (a certain day). Here are the steps taken:\n\nFirst, calculate the difference in days between the first day of May and the first replacement activity:\n165 days + 30 days + 14 days = 209 days.\n\nNext, find the day of the month for each subsequent battery replacement:\n- The 2nd battery gets replaced on the 210th day.\n- The 3rd battery gets replaced on the 211th day.\n- ...\n- The 25th battery will get replaced 25 - 1 = 24 advances of 7 days.\n\nTherefore, the 25th battery replacement date is:\n24 x 7 + 210 = 268 days.\n\nNow, find the month of the 268 days:\n- February has 28 + 30 + 31 = 89 days.\n- March has 31 + 28 + 30 = 90 days.\n- April has 30 days.\nSince 268 days fall into May, the 25th battery replacement will occur on May.\n\nThe final answer is May.",
